00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.570
What about Python 3 developers?

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.239
WESLEY: Yeah.

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:07.810
Until fall 2021, you couldn't
port the module 1 Flask app

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.930
to Python 3 because it uses
App Engine bundled services--

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.370
in this case, NDB.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.040
Once this feature
launched, Python 3 users

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.470
are now able to access many
of those services which

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.330
brought users to App Engine.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.000
We'll cover this new feature
in another video soon.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.860
But suffice it to say that
users can port the module 1

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.760
app to Python 3 first
or add Memcache,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.580
like we're going to do today,
and then upgrade to Python 3.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.020
Either way works.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.670
MARTIN: Sounds good, Wes.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.295
What are we going to use
Memcache for in our sample app?

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:38.170
WESLEY: I'm glad you
asked because I was just

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.430
about to get into that.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:42.700
As you know, our app creates a
new entity for each page visit.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.430
Because it only shows the
10 most recent visitors,

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.220
there's no need to create new
visits if the same user keeps

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.660
hitting our website, right?

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.730
So we'll just cache
the most recent visits

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.450
for an hour for the same user.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.110
If a new user comes along,
that will reset the cache.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:58.200
Also, the cache will
expire after an hour.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.240
Sound good?

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.610
MARTIN: OK.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.000
But I have to be honest.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.260
I haven't used App Engine
Memcache in quite a while.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.660
Can I get my hands
dirty and do it myself,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.580
while you are
showing us onscreen?

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.750
WESLEY: Absolutely.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.060
Go grab the module 1 code,
if you did the codelab,

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.790
or clone the repo or download
the ZIP file if you didn't.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:17.440
Pause here if you
need to do that.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.240
Module 1 is where we'll start.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.830
If you want to do
this by hand with me

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.830
now or on your own time,
follow the module 12 codelab.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:24.550
Ready?

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.982
Let's go to the computer
now and do this.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.190
Because it's always good to
start from a working app,

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:34.050
use gcloud app deploy to
redeploy your module 1 app

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.330
and ensure it works
before we update it.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.750
Python 3 users can delete
the appengine_config.py file

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.630
and relax for a bit, while
Python 2 developers install

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.750
the third-party libraries into
the lib folder with the pip

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.770
install command
you see onscreen.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.980
Then everyone can
use gcloud app deploy

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.020
to upload the app
to the cloud, then

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.480
confirm that that module
1 app still works.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.340
Now we can add
some caching to it.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.200
Before we make
changes, be aware you

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.240
won't see a difference
in output afterwards.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.300
Instead, we're just going to
avoid the extra Datastore calls

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.010
and see lower latency.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.810
With that out of
the way, let's start

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.310
with the imports at the top.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.710
All that's needed is to bring
in the App Engine Memcache

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.370
library.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.110
Since we're going to
cache for an hour,

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.310
add a constant for that.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.550
Register visits, querying for
the latest visits to display,

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.950
and other Datastore
calls stay the same.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.010
The biggest updates to the code
are in the main application.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.040
So visits are determined
by a visitor's IP address,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.360
along with a user agent.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.810
In the original app, we create
the visit entity immediately.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.750
In the update, we save
the visitor info first,

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.210
then try to get the latest
visits from the cache.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.550
If the cache is empty
or it's a new visitor,

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.470
save this as the newest visit.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.630
Fetch all the latest
visits from Datastore

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.360
and cache them for an hour,
in case the same visitor

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.660
comes back sooner.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.980
And that's all that's necessary
to change this app to add

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.820
caching to the module 1 app.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.920
So now just save and
gcloud app deploy

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.310
to see our updated
app in action.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.260
Again, the output
doesn't change,

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.110
but what you should notice
is that page refreshes

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.460
will be much quicker.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:05.320
Hit your app from
another computer

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.390
or wait for more
than an hour to see

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.490
that the app goes back
to its original latency

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.452
in fetching of the initial data.

00:04:11.452 --> 00:04:13.660
Now, before we get back to
the main part of the show,

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.993
